WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.130
Mining is one of the most dangerous professions
in the world, and while advances in technology

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:09.999
and safety protocols have certainly eased
the load that these hardened laborers endure,

00:00:09.999 --> 00:00:16.289
it still remains a daring, backbreaking endeavor,
where accidents do happen, and your safety

00:00:16.289 --> 00:00:20.949
is never one hundred percent guaranteed. But
mining is also a less common profession in

00:00:20.949 --> 00:00:26.550
the United States today, with mines incorporating
more technology and less overall manual labor.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:32.050
But it wasn’t always that way. In the 19th
and early 20th centuries, mining companies

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:36.570
employed hundreds of thousands of workers
across the country. Before large machinery

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:41.411
could mine surface pits and maneuver large
scale explosives from a safe distance, mining

00:00:41.411 --> 00:00:47.480
was done manually, performed by teams of thousands
of workers tirelessly slaving in the dark,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:53.629
digging for precious resources such as coal
or limestone, all while being underpaid, overworked,

00:00:53.629 --> 00:00:56.660
and continually endangered on the job.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:01.039
Mines were operated by mining companies, who
often took a large cut of a miner’s paycheck.

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:08.259
A 1902 account of a coal miner’s paycheck
claimed a $1.60 daily salary for a 10 hour

00:01:08.259 --> 00:01:14.390
shift. Even when adjusted for inflation today,
that only comes out to $4.50 an hour, which

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:19.530
is below the United States minimum wage. And
some of that money would be taxed, or given

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:25.360
to the company for providing housing for the
miners families in company towns located adjacent

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:30.520
to the mines. While some companies were better
than others in terms of safety, unionizing

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:35.060
and demanding better pay or conditions was
frowned upon, and there was always the risk

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:39.891
of being kicked out of the town by the company
if you were caught attempting to do so. Because

00:01:39.891 --> 00:01:45.040
of the demand and the cost of living, boys
as young as age 9 worked in mineshafts in

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.560
grueling conditions - this treatment was a
driving force in necessitating child labor

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:56.210
laws. And worst of all, accidents in the mines
were all too common in the early 20th century.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:02:01.170
Mining involves the usage of explosives to
carve out new sections of rock to mine, and

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:06.100
if something went wrong, it could have resulted
in a cave-in, the complete collapse of a mining

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:11.110
tunnel or the surrounding rock, where dozens
or potentially even hundreds of miners could

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:17.410
be injured or worse. You had to work in complete
darkness, save for a few well placed torches,

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:22.410
push a cumulative thousands of pounds of materials
every day, and contend with the ever present

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:27.630
risk of a gas leak, which could suffocate
workers in a cramped, narrow shaft or even

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:34.170
result in an explosion when coming into contact
with the materials used during blasting. In

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:40.640
1917, 2,696 coal mining deaths were recorded
as a result of various causes. And that was

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:45.810
just one year of many. The underground has
claimed countless lives as a result of human

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:51.450
greed prioritizing profits and material output
over safety. It’s an area of nature we were

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:56.200
never truly meant to interact with, and the
sheer number of things that can go wrong in

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:01.641
a mining operation proves that. With all of
this death, danger, and darkness, it’s no

00:03:01.641 --> 00:03:06.800
wonder that the mining industry is the center
of a blood-curdling anomaly that caught the

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:12.030
attention of the SCP Foundation. Today on
SCP Explained, we’ll be taking a look at

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:20.220
SCP-2951, an anomaly given the elusive codename
of “10,000 Years”. It will, as the channel’s

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:27.430
name implies, all be explained in due time.
The year is 1944. The Lemon Quarry, a limestone

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:32.320
mine located near Guthrie, Indiana, is like
countless others in the country. It’s owned

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:37.010
by the B.G Hoadley Mining Group, a company
that would soon find themselves with one less

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:42.480
mine to manage, and a lot of information to
cover up and destroy. Up until now, the operation

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.490
was proceeding smoothly, with the quarry’s
limestone deposits providing rich beds of

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:52.930
materials to export and sell, but all of that
was about to change. On August 23rd, 1944,

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:58.330
an earthquake occurred directly underneath
the Lemon Quarry. Seismic activity in Indiana

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:03.470
is strange enough, due to the area’s solid
limestone foundation and lack of fault lines,

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:08.030
but it was about to get a whole lot stranger.
Naturally, the company sent in an exploratory

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:12.560
team to assess the damage of the structure,
fearing that their limestone deposits were

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:18.350
caved-in or destroyed in the process. Three
hours later, the team returned to the surface,

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:22.980
reporting that an important access tunnel
had collapsed entirely. The tunnel was a necessary

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:27.310
section of the mineshaft, and the company
supervisors couldn’t afford to lose it,

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:31.010
so a larger team of workers were ordered to
clear the debris from the tunnel using their

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:36.310
hands and as much large machinery as they
could fit into the narrow shaft. During this

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:40.870
operation, another strange earthquake occurred,
causing a tunnel to collapse behind the crew

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:42.620
clearing the access tunnel.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:46.900
The quarry was sent into a panic. Another
team was sent in to remove debris and attempt

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:52.020
to free the initial clearing crew. After four
hours of tireless work, they were successful,

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:57.520
and the clearing crew was saved, but the original
access tunnel was still blocked. This is when

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:02.220
it gets strange. The crew also reported that,
due to the earthquake shifting the cavern,

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:06.840
a new tunnel, one that hadn’t been cut by
the mining group and was not charted in the

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:12.330
company’s records, was opened. During exploration
of this newly discovered tunnel, it was described

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:17.630
as being smoothly cut, and descending on a
slight decline. The mining company speculated

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:21.160
that this may have been a tunnel cut by a
mining group prior to the quarry’s purchase

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:25.810
by B.G Hoadley that wasn’t properly recorded.
They hoped it would connect around to the

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:30.960
primary, still-blocked tunnel, and so they
assembled another team of 23 men to use the

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:35.940
new passage to access the rear of the blockage
and determine whether or not the use of explosives

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.100
to gain re-entry into the blocked tunnel was
viable.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:43.760
And this is where the details of the story
run short. Sometime afterwards, there was

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:48.820
a third round of seismic activity, this time
collapsing the mine’s entrance tunnel. Over

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:53.030
the next three days, teams above ground removed
rubble and debris covering the entrance, and

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:57.970
the company’s supervisors attempted to contact
the men located underground using a telephone

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:02.980
cable line that ran into an access shaft in
the mine. On the evening of the third day,

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:03.980
just when the company was preparing to request
aid from other mining groups in the area,

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:09.080
an unknown individual emerged from the secondary
shaft and made it to the surface. What happened

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:13.960
next is unknown, but due to their collection
of information regarding the Lemon Quarry

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:19.500
incident, the Foundation discovered a single
telegraph, wired from the quarry to the mining

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.140
company’s head offices in Louisville. It
read:

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:27.150
26 8 1944
Mine abandoned. Tunnels remain collapsed.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:30.140
23 lost.
One of them came up the shaft. We tossed it

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:32.090
back down. Wasn't right.

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:37.560
Sometime after this, B.G Hoadley sold the
quarry, where it sat abandoned for decades,

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:42.930
and the events that occurred there remaining
hidden and forgotten until June 4th, 1998,

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:48.440
when low seismic activity was detected outside
of Foundation facility Site-81. Foundation

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:53.980
geologists were dispatched to assess the situation,
but were unable to determine much information,

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:58.520
including where the activity was coming from.
Two weeks later, a missing person report was

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:02.960
filed with local law enforcement, where a
15 year old boy disappeared after he and his

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:07.730
friends were trespassing in the Lemon Quarry.
While search efforts were conducted, the boy

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:11.971
remained missing. But during those searches
of the quarry, it was discovered that there

00:07:11.971 --> 00:07:16.520
was an unsealed shaft located beneath the
mine’s above ground maintenance building

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:22.560
that led directly into the mine itself.
A rescue team was lowered into the shaft,

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:26.970
after all, it was possible that the boy could
have fell in and was still down there. But

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:30.930
due to the unexpected depth and length of
the access tunnel, the team had to wait until

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:36.250
longer ropes and safety harnesses were available.
The estimated depth of the tunnel was 120

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:40.920
meters, but the rescue team reassessed those
numbers after exploring the shaft, finding

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:43.780
them to be closer to 240 meters.

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:48.960
Still, the boy was unable to be found, and
the rescue crews reported feeling agitated,

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:53.210
as well as having doubts about their perception
of the mine around them. The five man rescue

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:57.740
crew reported there being seven or eight members
of the team, and one of the men reported that

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:03.300
they were in the mine to “look for gold”
and not the missing boy. After 43 minutes,

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:08.130
the team went radio silent, and ceased responding
to communications. Above ground, the teams

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:12.699
retracted their tether, but found that more
was being retracted than had gone down the

00:08:12.699 --> 00:08:18.500
shaft. After retracting 400 meters of tether,
the winch was overwhelmed, and came to a stop.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:23.199
It was these events that alerted the SCP Foundation
about potential anomalous activity in the

00:08:23.199 --> 00:08:27.550
Lemon Quarry. The Foundation took control
of the rescue efforts, posing as a federal

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:32.180
search and rescue team. They were successful,
somewhat, retrieving two of the five men,

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:37.080
who were still connected to their tethers,
but less connected to their minds. One man

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:41.340
became violent when he reached the surface,
and began to physically attack Foundation

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:45.890
personnel, believing he was still deep within
the mine. The other man was originally believed

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:51.820
to be comatose, but after twenty minutes of
unconsciousness, he began speaking unintelligibly,

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:56.790
in a voice that wasn’t his own, but one
of the other men he went down into the shaft

00:08:56.790 --> 00:09:00.980
with. The three other men did not surface.
Two of their tethers returned with the ropes

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:06.270
clean cut on their side. The third was clearly
sliced with jagged pieces of rock, and covered

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:09.830
in human blood across a significant portion
of its length.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:13.870
After the two retrieved men were transported
to Site-81, the Foundation quickly administered

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:18.310
amnestics to all non-Foundation personnel,
and developed a cover story for the events

00:09:18.310 --> 00:09:24.029
that occurred. The Lemon Quarry was classified
as SCP-2951 for the interior of the mine being

00:09:24.029 --> 00:09:29.030
subject to irregular spatial and temporal
anomalies. A historical probe into the B.

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:36.380
G. Hoadley company and the 1944 incident was
launched, and inside SCP-2951, the Foundation

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:42.080
dispatched four members of the mobile task
force trotter-5, a squad named Hell’s Heroes,

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:46.300
to further analyze what was occurring in the
underground. The team entered the mine through

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:50.850
the secondary access shaft, and was ordered
to spend no longer than forty minutes in the

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:54.279
mine.
There was, though it remained unlikely, the

00:09:54.279 --> 00:09:58.370
slight chance that they could recover the
three lost search and rescue members and the

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:02.900
missing boy, though the Foundation wasn’t
holding their breath, knowing very well how

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:07.790
strange, mysterious, and dangerous anomalous
locations can be.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:11.700
The task force descended, and after a quick
mic check to determine that their recording

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:16.570
equipment was working, they moved further
down the shaft. It was dark, and unnaturally

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:22.410
deep. After reaching 120 meters, they came
to a stop, an area where they could walk around.

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:27.390
This contradicted the 240 meter depth reported
by the rescue team. The task force looked

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:32.180
for tether hooks, or any other physical evidence
from the original team, but they only found

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:36.830
footprints. Moving around the dark, winding
area, they began to explore. It wasn’t long

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:41.290
before the operatives became disoriented.
Keeping in mind their 40 minute limit, one

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:45.940
operative started the clock, and the captain
ordered him to let him know whenever 10 minutes

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:50.640
had passed. While exploring, they noticed
two tether lines up against a wall of rock.

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:55.080
They took pictures and moved on, descending
deeper. The timekeeping soldier reported that

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:59.390
they clocked in ten minutes, but the others
felt like it had been longer than that. Coming

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:04.360
to a narrow, tight access shaft, the team
determined that they needed to move single

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:05.360
file.

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:09.860
While significant time was passing, the timekeeper
only reported that they had been underground

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:15.200
for 17 minutes. Being skilled in anomalous
exploration, the team members realized that

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:21.300
there was something wrong, and that this was
most likely a temporal anomaly. But that wasn’t

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:26.120
all, the team began seeing flashes of light
in the distance, and hearing noises beneath

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:30.060
them. They made the decision to pull out of
the shaft, and after moving towards the light

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:34.310
in front of them, thinking it was from the
surface, they found that they were no closer

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:40.190
to leaving than they had been when they entered.
The clock still displayed a time of 17 minutes,

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:44.460
and trying to figure out where they were in
the shaft was becoming next to impossible.

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:48.980
As if it couldn’t get any worse, the team’s
flashlights and headlamps began dying out.

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:54.360
Now, the task force was completely in the
dark, and they could only move downwards.

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:58.880
They weren’t sure where they were going,
but they were certain that it was down. The

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:04.400
sensations of the cavern were growing stronger.
Strange smells. Something unclear written

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:09.950
on the walls of the cave. The clock now displayed
13 minutes. The operatives began repeating

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:16.010
themselves, stating the phrase “Too long
in the fire.” over and over again. It was

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:21.790
a nightmare, but the team soldiered onward,
dazed by the shaft’s anomalous effects.

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:25.300
Just when they were able to see the surface
light again, they noticed something. There

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:30.490
were more members of the team than they originally
started with. Three of them. Mimicking the

00:12:30.490 --> 00:12:35.320
others' voices, wearing their uniforms. One
of the entities appeared as if it were on

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:41.980
fire, smoke smoldering from its back. Repeating
that phrase over and over again. The captain

00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:46.250
ordered his men to shoot at the imposters,
firing at them in the dark. But the shots

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:51.010
missed, and accidentally hit something that
caused a violent combustion, causing all recording

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:56.300
devices to cut out, and the Foundation to
remove the task force from the shaft entirely.

00:12:56.300 --> 00:13:01.320
All four members were recovered, and given
a medical evaluation. The entities that impersonated

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:06.680
and attacked the task force, however, were
unable to be found. During an interview with

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:11.279
one of the recovered operatives, he claimed
that the team was losing track of time, but

00:13:11.279 --> 00:13:15.380
was shocked to discover that while their recorders
were active for a total of five hours and

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:21.890
thirty three minutes, they only spent 19 minutes
total in the mine altogether. A strange, anomalous

00:13:21.890 --> 00:13:26.470
time dilation effect between the surface and
the underground. The operative was unable

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:30.841
to determine the point when the entities,
clad in their armor and badges, joined up

00:13:30.841 --> 00:13:36.220
with the group. The interviewing doctor offered
the operative an amnestic, but he declined,

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:39.330
stating that he’ll only need it if he’s
still dreaming about the entity screaming

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:41.779
at him with his own voice months later.

00:13:41.779 --> 00:13:47.610
While the Foundation’s exploration of SCP-2951
revealed the anomalous effects of the shaft,

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:52.911
the historical investigation also bore fruit.
They learned the story of the 1944 collapse

00:13:52.911 --> 00:13:57.300
that caused B.G Hoadley to sell the mine,
but they also learned another important piece

00:13:57.300 --> 00:14:01.810
of information about the Lemon Quarry. The
Foundation recovered a contact list in an

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:07.149
abandoned Hoadley office that allowed the
Foundation to make contact with Gorman Ellis,

00:14:07.149 --> 00:14:11.850
a retired Hoadley investigator who was cooperative
and willing when met with Foundation agents

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:16.269
knocking on his door. During the interview,
the Foundation learned that Ellis was originally

00:14:16.269 --> 00:14:20.830
a foreman with the company, and both his father
and his grandfather were associated with the

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:25.270
higher ups at Hoadley. When asked about the
Lemon Quarry, Ellis said that while he never

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:29.720
worked there, he did spend time there cleaning
it up after the company had shut the mine

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:34.890
down. Ellis recognized how strange an earthquake
in the area was, but couldn’t put his finger

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:39.660
on anything strange about the collapse. He
knew they lost a few men during it, but the

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:44.089
incident wasn’t talked about much. He told
the agent to attempt to get a hold of a man

00:14:44.089 --> 00:14:49.060
by the last name of Barnes, who was also involved
in the cleanup and had contacts with the company

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:53.380
who bought out the land after Hoadley sold
it. Just when the Agent was about to leave,

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:56.580
however, Ellis remembered another piece of
information.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:15:00.910
The cleanup that he worked on had over three
dozen men working at the same time, but Ellis

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:06.390
said that it was the quietest job he had ever
worked. In fact, he wasn’t sure if a single

00:15:06.390 --> 00:15:10.620
one of them said anything to him the entire
time that he was there.

00:15:10.620 --> 00:15:14.269
The Foundation received a number of personal
documents from Ellis’s contact, Barnes,

00:15:14.269 --> 00:15:19.120
in the form of letters that detailed the Lemon
Quarry’s sale to Kervier International.

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:23.910
The incident was described as a typical cave-in,
but also detailed that strange men in suits

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:28.800
appeared at the scene weeks after, asking
questions and attempting to “listen to the

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:33.510
rocks”, according to the letter. After this,
Kervier International, a mining group that

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:38.490
the Foundation has so little information on
that they believe it is anomalous itself,

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:42.320
purchased the Lemon Quarry. A letter addressed
to barnes read as follows:

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:47.870
I saw it myself, Jeremiah. I saw something
that was like a man crawl out of that hole.

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:52.940
It smoked and burned and cried out in another's
voice. It was a thing pulled straight from

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:57.350
the Pit itself, I have no doubt.
That man from Geist said as much himself,

00:15:57.350 --> 00:16:01.760
that the pillars that support the world will
crack and crumble, and the foundation will

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:07.180
become loose. What lies below will become
accessible, and its might will fall upon the

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:11.760
meek. I saw it with my own eyes, I know it
is true.

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:18.360
I still hear its words, Jeremiah. "Ten thousand
years." Screaming like a wild dog, shrieking

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:21.620
like it was cornered. "Ten thousand years
in the fire."

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:27.839
In 2003, Ellis passed away, with the Foundation
seizing his assets. During this process, the

00:16:27.839 --> 00:16:31.160
Foundation discovered a letter addressed to
an unknown recipient, revealing that he knew

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:35.790
more about the Lemon Quarry than he had led
on. Its contents are chilling, reading:

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:41.060
It was twenty-three in total. Twenty-three
of those poor boys got stuck behind that wall.

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:45.529
We could hear them for days, shouting behind
those rocks while we sat around and did nothing.

00:16:45.529 --> 00:16:50.040
Have you ever been down in a mine during a
blackout? Let me tell you about it. First

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:54.480
there is a moment of panic, when everybody
scrambles to figure out what's going on. Then,

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:59.450
as things calm down, you try to get your eyes
adjusted to the dark around you. But you never

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:04.420
get adjusted, because there's nothing to see.
It's not like dark at night, where you can

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:09.889
see stars and the moon, or a streetlight.
There is no light in a mine during a blackout.

00:17:09.889 --> 00:17:14.640
There's nothing to see down there.
Then you start to hear things. Some boys will

00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:19.489
hear voices, or animals, or any number of
things that just aren't there. Some will wander

00:17:19.489 --> 00:17:24.390
off and get lost, they won't follow the ropes
back up. Some will fall in a shaft or into

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:28.100
a crevice, and you'll never see them again.
Then it gets real quiet.

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:33.100
I got to see that tunnel they found before
the cave-in. Very strange. Didn't look dug

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:37.630
by tools, not proper. Didn't even have time
to string up lights in it, to see where it

00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:42.720
went. I don't know what's down there. Anyway,
all I'm saying is, I haven't thought much

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:48.419
about Hell but I sure think we deserve it.
Whatever happens to those boys, as long as

00:17:48.419 --> 00:17:52.539
they’re down there, is our fault. It's our
fault for doing nothing.

00:17:52.539 --> 00:17:54.380
And the dark changes people.

00:17:54.380 --> 00:18:01.200
Now go watch “SCP-1179 - Centralian Fire
Demon” and “SCP–2935 – O, Death”

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:04.799
for more possible mine and cave-dwelling anomalies
from SCP Explained!

